---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service - Forward Design Consulting"
  description="The terms that govern use of the Forward Design Consulting website and how project engagements are defined."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="full">
      <div class="mv-rise" data-mv-watch>
        <p class="eyebrow"><span>Legal</span></p>
        <h1 class="display">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="lede">The basics that apply whether you're browsing this site or working with us on a project.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="full">
      <div class="container-prose legal-content mv-rise" data-mv-watch>
        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: August 8, 2026</p>

        <h2>Agreement to terms</h2>
        <p>
          By using this website, you agree to these terms with Forward Design Consulting
          LLC ("we," "us"). If you don't agree, please don't use the site. These terms
          cover the website itself; a separate written proposal governs the terms of any
          project we take on together.
        </p>

        <h2>Scope of engagement</h2>
        <p>
          Every project starts with a proposal specific to that engagement — pages,
          timeline, price, and what's included. That proposal, once accepted, is what
          defines the work. These general terms don't replace it; they sit alongside it.
        </p>

        <h2>No guaranteed outcomes</h2>
        <p>
          We build websites we're proud of, but we can't guarantee specific business
          results — traffic, leads, rankings, or revenue. Too much of that depends on
          factors outside a website's design: your market, your follow-through, and plain
          luck.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Ownership of the final website design and files transfers to the client once
          the project is paid in full. Until then, the work remains ours.
        </p>

        <h2>Website use</h2>
        <p>
          Content on this site — text, images, and design — belongs to Forward Design
          Consulting LLC unless noted otherwise, and is here to inform you about our
          work. You're welcome to link to it; please don't copy it wholesale for your
          own site.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          This website and its content are provided as-is. To the extent allowed by law,
          Forward Design Consulting isn't liable for damages arising from your use of this
          site. For work we've been engaged to do, liability is limited as set out in the
          relevant project proposal.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms as the studio grows. Continued use of the site after a
          change means you accept the update.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms? Email
          <a href="mailto:fwddesignconsulting@gmail.com">fwddesignconsulting@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-content p.legal-meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-step--2);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  .legal-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 60;
    font-size: var(--text-step-3);
    color: var(--color-navy);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal-content h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal-content p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-fg-soft);
  }
  .legal-content a {
    color: var(--color-blue);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong);
  }
  .legal-content a:hover {
    color: var(--color-navy);
  }
</style>
